# INVWINWA.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY: Split units at
# level 3.  On the item list with item 2 (two Tandon drives) selected,
# Record > Split units (ALT-C U) opens the dialog "Split item 2" with the
# one field Quantity.  0 is
# refused with "bad or missing argument" on the message line, the focus
# staying on Quantity; a letter is no number; six digits are cut to five,
# more than are on hand; 1 splits off item 4, the list refetched with the
# selection kept, the status bar "Split off item 4".
# The Record menu's "Split units" opens the dialog for the row selected,
# also on a location's contents and on search results, where the one unit
# of item 2 is not enough for a split of one.  With no row (an empty
# result) the entry is grayed and choosing it does nothing; an item's
# parts screen has no such entry, so U finds nothing there.  The end by Exit.
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINWA.SNP is its snapshot.
T ADMIN
K TAB
T Retro1986
K ENTER
S ITEMS
K DOWN ALT-C U
S DIALOG
T 0
K ENTER
S ZERO
# a letter is refused as no number, six digits are cut to five, which
# are more than are on hand
K DEL
T x
K ENTER
S LETTER
K DEL
T 123456
S LIMIT
K ENTER
S TOOMANY
K DEL
T 1
K ENTER
S SPLIT
# item 4 is a row of the list; the Record menu holds the entry after
# Take out, and chooses the dialog for the row selected
K DOWN DOWN DOWN
S NEWROW
K ALT-C
S MENU
K ESC ESC
K ALT-C U
S MENUDLG
K ESC
S MENUESC
# the same on a location's contents
K ESC ALT-L B
S LOCS
K ENTER
S CONTENTS
K DOWN
K ALT-C U
S CONTDLG
K ESC
S CONTESC
K ESC ESC
# search results
K ALT-S T
T Tandon
K ENTER
S FOUND
K ALT-C U
S FNDDLG
T 1
K ENTER
S FNDSPLIT
K ESC ESC
# an empty result, from the search dialog that ESC opened again: the
# entry is grayed and choosing it does nothing
T nothing-like-this
K ENTER
S EMPTY
K ALT-C
S EMPMENU
K ESC ESC
K ALT-C U
S EMPTYF9
K ESC ESC
# on an item's parts U finds no entry
K HOME ALT-C P
S PARTS
K ALT-C U
S PARTSF9
K ESC ESC
K ALT-C
S PRTMENU
K ESC ESC
K ALT-F X
